  "interpretation": [
    "The primary graph covariance initialization does not show a consistent aggregate MRR advantage over the fixed controls on these three source-selected VALID banks.",
    "Graph MRR is lower in all three seeds versus TabM-style first normal, random signs all, and copied independent warm four. Graph versus feature covariance and single has two negative seeds and one positive seed; versus warm identity has one negative and two positive seeds.",
    "Graph versus warm identity has a positive mean MRR delta but lower Hit10 in every seed. All paired exploratory df2 intervals cross zero.",
    "Graph members remain competent at their pooled source-selected checkpoint (mean member MRR 0.271067, mean minimum member MRR 0.265933), but mean pooling gain is only 0.000633 and common shared-competitor errors remain nearly coincident across members.",
    "Copied independent warm four has lower mean member MRR 0.259492 but larger pooling gain 0.023042 and fewer all-member/common-slot errors. It shares one warm donor and a pooled selector and pays four full member trajectories; it is not four independently acquired donors or evidence that the graph initialization is necessary.",
    "Graph repairs some baseline common errors, while regressions and reciprocal-rank losses elsewhere prevent an aggregate gain. Baseline common-error cohorts alone are conditional diagnostics, not a stand-alone success criterion.",
    "Feature covariance uses graph-derived H and is not a graph-free control. These are initialization arms; no growth capacity/necessity inference is established by this initialization-only read.",
    "Three optimizer seeds on one fixed graph/split give conditional optimizer-seed dispersion only. VALID selector optimism remains after twelve exposures, first strict rounded4 maximum, and no reselection. Queries are not iid graph replications; no graph-population CI or significance claim is made.",
    "All selected rounded4 maximum tie lists are singleton in this retrieved initialization family. Full60 completion remains required even where the selected checkpoint is early.",
    "Warm1 process exit remains unknown under admitted terminal20 artifact custody. Its source-inclusive cost is counted, but unmeasured upstream failed/orphan-owner and recovery wall time remains unknown."
  ],
